    "morphemes": [],
    "sources": [
      {
        "quote": "From Middle Chinese 缽 (MC pat, “bowl; basin; pot”), itself shortened from 缽多羅 (MC pat ta la, “monk's alms bowl”), a transcription of Sanskrit पात्र (pātra, “a drinking vessel, goblet, bowl, cup, dish, pot, plate, utensil; any vessel or receptacle”). Ultimately tracing back to Proto-Indo-European *peh₃- (“to drink”), and thus cognate with the pot- portion of English potable."
      },
      {
        "quote": "First attested in Japanese in the Nihon Shoki of 720 CE."
